# 1992 TIGER/Line fixtures are fixed-width ASCII with CRLF record
# terminators (matching real Census files) and a binary zip. The repo's
# top-level `* text=auto` strips the \r from CRLF line endings on commit,
# which silently shrinks every fixture below its documented byte count
# (verified: TGR34999.F51 460 -> 458 bytes once normalized). Every byte
# count in test/sql/tiger1992_zip.test and the task brief depends on these
# staying byte-exact, so this whole tree is marked binary: no line-ending
# or encoding conversion, ever, on any platform.
* -text
